ept a single artifact object or an array."},"659":{"id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing-60","page_id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing#schema-loading","content":"Flag"},"660":{"id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing-61","page_id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing#schema-loading","content":"Description"},"661":{"id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing-62","page_id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing#schema-loading","content":"`--schema <path\\|url>`"},"662":{"id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing-63","page_id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing#schema-loading","content":"JSON Schema file (local path or HTTP/HTTPS URL)."},"663":{"id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing-64","page_id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing#schema-loading","content":"`--schema-json <json>`"},"664":{"id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing-65","page_id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing#schema-loading","content":"Inline JSON Schema string."},"665":{"id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing-66","page_id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing#schema-loading","content":"Schema loading from URLs sends `Accept: application/schema+json, application/json` headers."},"666":{"id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing-67","page_id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing#custom-parsers","content":"There are three ways to extend Struktur with support for new file formats:"},"667":{"id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing-68","page_id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing#custom-parsers","content":"**Configuration-level (recommended):** `struktur config parsers add` — zero code, works in CLI and SDK via `parserConfig`"},"668":{"id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing-69","page_id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing#custom-parsers","content":"**SDK-level inline parser:** Add an `InlineParserDef` to `parserConfig` — code-only, works with `parse()`"},"669":{"id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing-70","page_id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing#custom-parsers","content":"**Legacy providers:** Use the deprecated `providers` registry with `fileToArtifact()`"},"670":{"id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing-71","page_id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing#option-1-configuration-level-recommended","content":"Register a parser by MIME type using the CLI. This works transparently for all `--input` and `parse` calls."},"671":{"id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing-72","page_id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing#option-1-configuration-level-recommended","content":"See config parsers for the full reference."},"672":{"id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing-73","page_id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing#option-1-configuration-level-recommended","content":"For the SDK, pass a `parserConfig` to `parse`:"},"673":{"id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing-74","page_id":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/document-parsing#option-2-sdk-level-inline-parser","content":"Add an `InlineParserDef` to your `parserConfig`. This is the modern way to register code-only parsers that work with `parse()`."},"67