","content":"Inputs and Artifacts"},"798":{"id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline-2","page_id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/explanation/pipeline#the-strategy-layer","content":"The Strategy layer"},"799":{"id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline-3","page_id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/explanation/pipeline#validation-inside-the-loop","content":"Validation inside the loop"},"800":{"id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline-4","page_id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/explanation/pipeline#the-result","content":"The result"},"801":{"id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline-5","page_id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/explanation/pipeline#see-also","content":"See also"},"802":{"id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline-6","page_id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/pipeline#inputs-and-artifacts","content":"Struktur converts input files into **Artifacts** before extraction. For plain text or stdin, this is trivial. For structured files (PDFs, Office documents), Struktur runs a parser — built-in or custom — that extracts text and images per-page."},"803":{"id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline-7","page_id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/pipeline#inputs-and-artifacts","content":"<Card title=\"Document Parsing\" description=\"Learn how files are converted to artifacts\" href=\"/docs/explanation/document-parsing\" />"},"804":{"id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline-8","page_id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/pipeline#inputs-and-artifacts","content":"<Card title=\"Artifact Format\" description=\"Understand the artifact data structure\" href=\"/docs/explanation/artifact-format\" />"},"805":{"id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline-9","page_id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/pipeline#the-strategy-layer","con