d":"/docs/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/quickstart#configure-your-api-key","content":"The `--default` flag automatically queries the provider API and sets the cheapest available model as default, so `--model` becomes optional in all future commands."},"1242":{"id":"/docs/quickstart-16","page_id":"/docs/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/quickstart#configure-your-api-key","content":"Output: `{ \"provider\": \"openai\", \"stored\": \"keychain\" }` (or `\"file\"` on Linux)."},"1243":{"id":"/docs/quickstart-17","page_id":"/docs/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/quickstart#set-a-default-model-if-not-using---default","content":"Once set, `--model` is optional in all `extract` commands."},"1244":{"id":"/docs/quickstart-18","page_id":"/docs/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/quickstart#extract-your-first-data","content":"The `--fields` flag builds a JSON Schema on the fly. Each field defaults to `string`; append `:number`, `:integer`, `:bool`, etc. to set the type. See Fields Shorthand for the full syntax."},"1245":{"id":"/docs/quickstart-19","page_id":"/docs/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/quickstart#extract-your-first-data","content":"If you need more control (optional fields, nested objects), pass a full schema instead:"},"1246":{"id":"/docs/quickstart-20","page_id":"/docs/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/quickstart#extract-your-first-data","content":"Notice that `total` is a number, not a string — Struktur enforced the schema."},"1247":{"id":"/docs/quickstart-21","page_id":"/docs/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/quickstart#what-happened","content":"For the text example, stdin input was loaded as an artifact, the LLM generated output, and it was validated against your schema. The `simple` strategy handled this in a single LLM call."},"1248":{"id":"/docs/quickstart-22","page_id":"/docs/quickstart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/quickstart#what-happened","co