"],[1673,"Struktur Documentation"],[1086,"Struktur does all of this for you."],[1136,"Struktur fills the gap: a focused extraction engine with an **autonomous agent** that handles the orchestration so you can focus on the output."],[1129,"Struktur is an all-in-one tool for structured data extraction using an **autonomous agent**. It turns documents into validated, schema-typed JSON by having an LLM agent explore the content, decide what to read, and build the output incrementally."],[735,"Struktur is built on the Vercel AI SDK, which provides a unified interface to multiple LLM providers. This architecture makes it straightforward to use any model from supported providers—or add new ones."],[63,"Struktur is published as an npm package and runs on Node.js 20 or newer. Install it in your image; there is no standalone binary to download."],[475,"Struktur only cares about what is in the artifact, not where it came from."],[1459,"Struktur provides an Agent Skill that teaches AI coding assistants (like Claude Code, OpenCode, Codex, etc.) how to use Struktur effectively."],[761,"Struktur supports two authentication methods:"],[1100,"Struktur uses **lenient validation** during intermediate extraction steps:"],[544,"Struktur validates artifact JSON before processing. Use the CLI:"],[1714,"Struktur vs Alternatives"],[625,"Struktur's parser system converts files into Artifact format before any LLM work happens. Parsers are resolved by MIME type and are fully configurable."],[1475,"Support"],[693,"Supported input kinds:"],[723,"Supported Providers"],[112,"Supported providers: `openai`, `anthropic`, `google`, `opencode`, `openrouter`."],[1456,"Supported Tools"],[3,"Synopsis"],[94,"Synopsis"],[157,"Synopsis"],[286,"Synopsis"],[354,"Synopsis"],[1354,"Target width in pixels (overrides `screenshotScale`)"],[427,"Test a schema against samples"],[1010,"Testing or prototyping"],[697,"Text artifact (split on double newlines)"],[1324,"Text artifact (split on double newlines)"],[515,"Text